---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Workplace Ergonomics Guide';
const description = 'A practical workplace ergonomics guide covering posture, movement breaks, desk setup, mobility and recovery for office and remote workers.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Workplace Wellness</div><h1>Workplace ergonomics guide for healthier workdays.</h1><p class="lead">Ergonomics is not only about the perfect chair. It is about building a work environment and movement routine that helps the body feel better throughout the day.</p></div></section>
<section class="content"><div class="container"><article>

<h2>Start with the basics</h2><p>A good ergonomic setup should reduce unnecessary strain. The screen should be easy to see, the keyboard and mouse should feel natural, and the feet should be supported. Small changes can make long workdays easier on the neck, shoulders, back and hips.</p><h2>Movement matters more than one perfect posture</h2><p>No posture is perfect forever. The body needs position changes, short walks, mobility breaks and simple strength work. A workplace wellness app can guide employees through short routines that fit between meetings.</p><h2>Simple office mobility routine</h2><ul><li>Neck and shoulder resets.</li><li>Thoracic rotations.</li><li>Hip flexor mobility.</li><li>Glute activation.</li><li>Wrist and forearm mobility.</li></ul><h2>How companies can use this</h2><p>Pair ergonomic education with guided movement sessions. Employees should know how to set up their workspace and what to do when their body feels stiff or tired.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Content angle:</strong> This page should connect the topic back to the app naturally. Mention guided training, body care, nutrition education and mental performance where relevant without forcing a sales pitch.</div>
</article></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
